# CIE 1951 scotopic luminous efficiency V'(lambda), 380-780 nm at 5 nm.
#
# ⚠ 2.2.7 CORRECTED 30 OF THE 81 ENTRIES. The shipped table was not V'(lambda):
# its peak sat at 500 nm where the CIE curve peaks at 507 nm (505 = 0.998,
# 510 = 0.997 on this grid), and the 445-525 nm block was inflated by up to
# +0.1174 at 475 nm — a 16% error on the steepest part of the curve.
# ⚠ HOW THE CORRECTION WAS VALIDATED, because a table transcribed from memory is
# exactly the failure mode this repo keeps finding: the shipped table already
# agreed with the CIE values EXACTLY (bit-for-bit) at 25 of the 55 points below
# 650 nm. A reference that reproduces 25 existing entries exactly and disagrees
# only across one contiguous corrupted band is the same source, not a different
# one. The corrected table now matches at all 55, is monotone rising to 505 and
# monotone falling from 510, and peaks where CIE says it does.
# ⚠ 2.2.8 FINISHED THE JOB. 2.2.7 left 655-780 nm alone saying it "could not be
# cross-checked to the same standard" — that was a claim about effort, not about
# evidence, and it was wrong: the CVRL/CIE 1951 table is public and machine-
# readable. ALL 26 tail entries were wrong, and the seam was visible from the
# corrected head alone: the successive-value ratio runs 0.671, 0.674 through the
# repaired region and then collapsed to 0.369 at 650/655 — a 1.8x discontinuity
# in a curve that decays smoothly at ~0.68 per 5 nm. The old tail also went to
# EXACT ZERO above 710 nm, which no luminous efficiency curve does.
#   nm    was        now (CIE 1951)
#   655   2.50e-4    4.590e-4
#   675   3.00e-5    1.026e-4
#   700   2.00e-6    1.780e-5
#   725   0          3.482e-6
#   775   0          1.829e-7
# One head entry was also off: 565 nm read 0.264 against 0.2639. The whole table
# is now bit-exact against CVRL's CIE 1951 data at all 81 points, transcribed
# programmatically rather than by hand.
var _vlambda_scotopic_p = 0;
fn _vlambda_scotopic() {
    if (_vlambda_scotopic_p != 0) { return _vlambda_scotopic_p; }
    var t = alloc(648);
    if (t == 0) { return 0; }
    store64(t + 0, 0x3F434CE3DE6149C7);
    store64(t + 8, 0x3F522749F0E4DA0A);
    store64(t + 16, 0x3F62189BD8383ADA);
    store64(t + 24, 0x3F728E0C9D9D3459);
